d 'VARORDER': module for automatic semantic temporal ordering of variables in wide-format Stata datasets
d
d  varorder automatically detects and reorganizes eligible temporal
d variable families in wide-format Stata datasets. The module uses
d semantic information in variable names, variable labels, variable
d notes, and attached value-label metadata; recognizes supported
d ordinary, staged, and hierarchical temporal sequences; and
d normalizes harmless differences in capitalization, separators,
d punctuation, and leading zeros internally. Attached value labels
d provide conservative value-domain or construct evidence but do
d not by themselves assign a variable-level time position.
d Ambiguous, conflicting, colliding, related but non-temporal, and
d unsupported cases are left unchanged. Before changing physical
d variable order, varorder displays one bounded consolidated
d preview and asks for a single Enter confirmation. This module
d changes only physical variable order, preserves data and
d metadata, applies the proposed permutation transactionally, and
d provides a single-level undo. 
d
d KW: data management
d KW: variable order
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260822
d
d Author: Hao Ma,  NA
d Support: email shouhuoxiwang2027@@gmail.com
d
f varorder.ado
f varorder.sthlp
